er go out of control or fall completely dormant, causing chaos in the World. Seeing this, Vishnu killed Kavyamata, freeing Indra and the others from her curse.<br /> <br /> The Rishi Bhrigu (composer of various hymns in the Rig Veda), Shukra's father and Kavayamata's husband, was angered at Vishnu's murder of his wife, especially given that Indra and his court had attacked without provocation, and cursed Vishnu to be be born on Earth and know the pain of separation form the one he loved. This is given as an explanation for why Rama and Sita, human avatara of Vishnu and Lakshmi, go through such long periods of separation. (Bhrigu brings Kavayamata back to life, btw, in case you're wondering, because Rishis can pretty much do anything in Hinduism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,thank you. That's fascinating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:53:51-07:00","id":1073657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070494-mythological-questions-thread?p=1071909#post1071909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aztecs are your big one here, and I would suggest mixing Moon and Stars into a single Titanrealm. It is just a good, solid solution, and makes sense for the Moon and Stars Titans to be in roughly a similar place. I believe Gotham By Night called the Titanrealm they made combining Moon and Stars Tamoachan back when their website was still up. Doing it this way solves a huge amount of difficulties, since the Aztecs issue is specifically with the night sky, including both the stars, and the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I never liked fusing the Moon and the Stars together. I can agree that both are <b>important </b>and <b>bad </b>in Aztec mythology, but they're distinct concepts and shouldn't have ther uniqueness taken away like that.<br /> <br /> Still, they are similar enough that I don't think it's the worst solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}